IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `ind-a-tests-fixtures`
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g3-licensee-duties`
IMPORT `g3-training-duty`
IMPORT `g3-operator`

-- ind-a-tests-s12-s18.l4: independent tests by ind-a for ss.12 to 18 (the licensee's and the operator's duties).
-- Expected values decided before the encoding was opened (work/ind-a/expectations.md, S12-* to S18-*).
-- Stated assumptions: the Law has commenced for the work; the act is work on a cooling system; the licensee
-- holds a grade 2 licence in force unless a scenario says otherwise.

§ `ind-a fixtures for ss.12 to 18`

`ind-a grade 2 in force` MEANS LIST `grade 2 licence`
`ind-a the licence` MEANS `ind-a plain licence` (YMD 2025 9 1) `grade 2 licence`

`ind-a installation work` MEANS
    `Work item` WITH
        `performed by` IS `ind-a person`
        `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
        `the system` IS (`Cooling system` WITH `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 10, `refrigerants` IS EMPTY)
        `date performed` IS YMD 2027 3 1

GIVEN part4 IS A BOOLEAN
      part5 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`ind-a standard findings` part4 part5 MEANS
    LIST (`Wording of Israeli Standard 994` WITH
              `the day this wording took effect` IS YMD 2020 1 1
              `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS part4
              `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS part4
              `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS part5)

GIVEN orderer IS A BOOLEAN
      demanded IS A BOOLEAN
      failed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Demand to see the licence`
`ind-a demand to see` orderer demanded failed MEANS
    `Demand to see the licence` WITH
        `the person demanding ordered the work` IS orderer
        `the person demanded to see the licence` IS demanded
        `the licensee failed to show the licence on the demand` IS failed

GIVEN change IS A DATE
      notice IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Change in the application particulars`
`ind-a change on` change `notified on` notice MEANS
    `Change in the application particulars` WITH
        `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application` IS TRUE
        `the day of the change` IS change
        `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying` IS FALSE
        `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed` IS FALSE
        `the day the notice was given to the Registrar` IS JUST notice

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      hours IS A NUMBER
      recognised IS A BOOLEAN
      field IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Training session attended`
`ind-a session on` day hours recognised field MEANS
    `Training session attended` WITH
        `the day attended` IS day
        `the licence was in force on the day attended` IS TRUE
        `hours attended` IS hours
        `held under the supervision of the Ministry` IS TRUE
        `conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS recognised
        `within the licensee's field of work under the licence` IS field
        `held on a date the Registrar directed` IS TRUE
        `attended because the Registrar required that particular course under section 17(b)` IS FALSE
        `the licensee met the requirements of the training` IS TRUE

-- The licence expires 2030-03-31 (granted 2025-09-01): its last year of validity ends that day.
`ind-a expiry` MEANS YMD 2030 3 31

GIVEN fixed IS A DATE
      unfulfilled IS A BOOLEAN
      consulted IS A BOOLEAN
      special IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Extension of validity under section 17(c)`
`ind-a extension to` fixed unfulfilled consulted special MEANS
    `Extension of validity under section 17(c)` WITH
        `the day of the Registrar's decision` IS YMD 2030 3 1
        `the last day of validity before any extension under section 17(c)` IS `ind-a expiry`
        `the last day of validity as it stands when the decision is taken` IS `ind-a expiry`
        `the last day of validity fixed by the extension` IS fixed
        `the licensee had not fulfilled the duty under section 17(a) or (b)` IS unfulfilled
        `the Council was consulted about the extension` IS consulted
        `the Council's advice about the extension was validly given` IS consulted
        `in the Registrar's opinion these are special cases and the circumstances are justified` IS special
        `the extension is granted so that the licensee can fulfil the duty` IS TRUE

GIVEN justified IS A BOOLEAN
      reasonable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Particular course required under section 17(b)`
`ind-a particular course` justified reasonable MEANS
    `Particular course required under section 17(b)` WITH
        `the day of the course` IS YMD 2027 6 1
        `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS YMD 2027 4 1
        `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS TRUE
        `the Council was consulted about requiring the course` IS TRUE
        `the Council's advice about requiring the course was validly given` IS TRUE
        `in the Registrar's opinion circumstances justify requiring attendance` IS justified
        `in the Registrar's opinion attendance is required to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law` IS justified
        `notice was given a reasonable time before the date of the course` IS reasonable
        `the licensee attended the course` IS TRUE
        `the licensee met the requirements of the course` IS TRUE

GIVEN regular IS A BOOLEAN
      business IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems`
`ind-a engager` regular business MEANS
    `Facts about a person who engages others in work on cooling systems` WITH
        `engages another person on a regular basis to perform work on cooling systems` IS regular
        `owns or manages a business that offers the performance of work on cooling systems to the public` IS business

GIVEN regular IS A BOOLEAN
      business IS A BOOLEAN
      held IS A LIST OF `Licence kind`
      kw IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a operator breaches 18(a)` regular business held kw MEANS
    `s.18(a) — the operator breached section 18(a)` (`ind-a engager` regular business) TRUE TRUE held
        (`licence kinds that cover a cooling system` (`Cooling system` WITH `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS kw, `refrigerants` IS EMPTY))

§ `s.12`

-- S12-01
#ASSERT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `ind-a the licence` `ind-a other person` `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.12 — permitting the person to use the licence breaches section 12` `ind-a the licence` `ind-a other person` `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE
-- S12-02: no other person is involved.
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — permitting the person to use the licence breaches section 12` `ind-a the licence` `ind-a person` `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE

§ `s.13`

-- S13-01, S13-02
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `ind-a installation work` (`ind-a standard findings` FALSE TRUE) TRUE `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `ind-a installation work` (`ind-a standard findings` TRUE FALSE) TRUE `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `ind-a installation work` (`ind-a standard findings` TRUE TRUE) TRUE `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE

§ `s.14`

-- S14-01, S14-02, S14-03
#ASSERT `s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` (`ind-a demand to see` TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` (`ind-a demand to see` TRUE FALSE TRUE) TRUE `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` (`ind-a demand to see` FALSE TRUE TRUE) TRUE `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` (`ind-a demand to see` TRUE TRUE FALSE) TRUE `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE

§ `s.15`

-- S15-01: a demand within the Registrar's power binds the licensee to comply.
#ASSERT `s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand` (`Demand of the Registrar under section 15` WITH `the kind of demand` IS `information or documents needed to realise the purposes of the Law`, `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS TRUE, `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS TRUE, `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS FALSE, `the day of the demand` IS YMD 2027 1 10, `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS NOTHING) `ind-a grade 2 in force` TRUE

§ `s.16`

-- S16-01, S16-02
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`ind-a change on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `notified on` (YMD 2026 4 9)) `ind-a no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`ind-a change on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `notified on` (YMD 2026 4 10)) `ind-a no rest days`
-- S16-03, S16-04
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`ind-a change on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `notified on` (YMD 2026 1 31)) `ind-a no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`ind-a change on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `notified on` (YMD 2026 2 1)) `ind-a no rest days`
-- S16-05, S16-06 (Saturday 2026-01-31 a rest day; IL s.10(c) applied to a deadline)
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`ind-a change on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `notified on` (YMD 2026 2 1)) `ind-a Saturdays`
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`ind-a change on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `notified on` (YMD 2026 2 2)) `ind-a Saturdays`
-- S16-07
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`ind-a change on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `notified on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `ind-a no rest days`
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `ind-a no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 9

§ `s.17`

-- S17-01, S17-02
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `ind-a session on` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE TRUE) `ind-a expiry` `ind-a expiry`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `ind-a session on` (YMD 2029 10 1) 7.5 TRUE TRUE) `ind-a expiry` `ind-a expiry`
-- S17-03: cumulative hours.
#ASSERT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `ind-a session on` (YMD 2029 6 1) 4 TRUE TRUE, `ind-a session on` (YMD 2029 11 1) 4 TRUE TRUE) `ind-a expiry` `ind-a expiry`
-- S17-04: outside the last year.
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `ind-a session on` (YMD 2028 12 1) 8 TRUE TRUE) `ind-a expiry` `ind-a expiry`
-- S17-05, S17-06
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `ind-a session on` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 FALSE TRUE) `ind-a expiry` `ind-a expiry`
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(a) — the training duty of section 17(a) was met` (LIST `ind-a session on` (YMD 2029 10 1) 8 TRUE FALSE) `ind-a expiry` `ind-a expiry`
-- S17-07, S17-08: three months after 2030-03-31 is 2030-06-30 (June lacks the 31st).
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`ind-a extension to` (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`ind-a extension to` (YMD 2030 7 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT `s.17(c) — the latest last day of validity after an extension of up to three months from` `ind-a expiry` EQUALS YMD 2030 6 30
-- S17-09, S17-10
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`ind-a extension to` (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE FALSE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`ind-a extension to` (YMD 2030 6 30) TRUE TRUE FALSE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(c) — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` (`ind-a extension to` (YMD 2030 6 30) FALSE TRUE TRUE) TRUE
-- S17-11
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` (`ind-a particular course` TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the Registrar has the power to require attendance at the course` (`ind-a particular course` FALSE TRUE) TRUE
-- S17-12: the duty to attend arises only on notice a reasonable time before the course.
#ASSERT `s.17(b) — the licensee must attend the course` (`ind-a particular course` TRUE TRUE) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(b) — the licensee must attend the course` (`ind-a particular course` TRUE FALSE) TRUE
-- S17-13: an unmet s.17(a) duty is a breach of a licence condition once the last day has passed.
#ASSERT `s.17(d) — the licensee breached a licence condition through the training duty as at` (YMD 2030 4 1) (LIST `ind-a session on` (YMD 2029 10 1) 7.5 TRUE TRUE) `ind-a expiry` `ind-a expiry` EMPTY TRUE
-- S17-14: (f) publication a reasonable time before; none published is not compliance.
#ASSERT `s.17(f) — the Registrar published the training in good time` (`Training offered` WITH `the day of the training` IS YMD 2029 6 1, `the day it was published on the Ministry website` IS JUST (YMD 2029 5 1), `the publication was a reasonable time before the training` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(f) — the Registrar published the training in good time` (`Training offered` WITH `the day of the training` IS YMD 2029 6 1, `the day it was published on the Ministry website` IS NOTHING, `the publication was a reasonable time before the training` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `s.17(e) — the Registrar has ensured that the trainings exist and are available` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.17(e) — the Registrar has ensured that the trainings exist and are available` TRUE FALSE

§ `s.18`

-- S18-01
#ASSERT `ind-a operator breaches 18(a)` TRUE FALSE EMPTY 10
-- S18-02, S18-03, S18-04
#ASSERT `ind-a operator breaches 18(a)` TRUE FALSE (LIST `grade 1 licence`) 50
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a operator breaches 18(a)` TRUE FALSE (LIST `grade 2 licence`) 50
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a operator breaches 18(a)` TRUE FALSE (LIST `grade 3 licence`) 50
-- S18-05: a one-off engager is not an operator.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a operator breaches 18(a)` FALSE FALSE EMPTY 10
-- S18-06
#ASSERT `s.18(c) — the person is an operator` (`ind-a engager` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-a operator breaches 18(a)` FALSE TRUE EMPTY 10
-- S18-07: the operator's own licence is no part of s.18(a); a properly licensed worker means no breach.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-a operator breaches 18(a)` TRUE TRUE (LIST `grade 1 licence`) 10
-- S18-08
#ASSERT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` (`ind-a engager` TRUE FALSE) TRUE TRUE (LIST `grade 2 licence`) (`Measures the operator took under section 18(b)` WITH `the measures were sufficient to make sure that the licensee would work to the Standard` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s.18(b) — the operator breached section 18(b)` (`ind-a engager` TRUE FALSE) TRUE TRUE (LIST `grade 2 licence`) (`Measures the operator took under section 18(b)` WITH `the measures were sufficient to make sure that the licensee would work to the Standard` IS TRUE)
